####  Nucleotide diversity (Pi) ####
## To calculate PI, you can need a VCF file and a file including the sample IDs that are used in the VCF file.
## PI, aka the nucleotide diversity (π), is the average number of nucleotide differences per site between two sequences, within a population:
## the total pairwise differences at all sites / number of pairwise comparisons × number of sites

## To extract the IDs, we can use
bcftools query -l your_file.vcf.gz > samples.txt
## Then, we check the samples.txt and allocate them manually. The final tab-separated file should look something like, e.g.:
sample  population
ind1    spA
ind2    spA
ind3    spA
ind4    spB
ind5    spB
ind6    spB

## We will calculate PI using both for the whole-genome and sliding windows:
## We use sinteractive with the default settings for this:
## Whole genome, per species do
